# Intentionally NO catch-all "/*  /index.html  200" rule.
#
# Every real route is prerendered at build time (dist/<route>/index.html), which Netlify serves
# directly. Unknown URLs therefore fall through to dist/404.html, which Netlify returns with a
# real HTTP 404 status (a catch-all 200 rewrite would turn every bad URL into a soft 404 that
# serves the homepage). Client-side navigation is unaffected: the router handles in-app links
# in the browser, and the 404 page hydrates and renders the same NotFound UI.
